        "receipt": "action.done"
      },
      "waitFor": {
        "pointer": "/topology/topology/focus/workspace",
        "equals": "$step:w4#/created/0",
        "maxMs": 5000
      },
      "checkpoint": [
        "turn",
        "settled"
      ],
      "note": "Cmd-9 selects the last workspace (sidebar.cmd9 last): w4"
    }
  ],
  "invariants": [
    "converted from scripts/cmux-next/chrome-tab-keys-e2e.py, which stays as the live check; tests/oracle/corpus/e2e/coverage.json maps the script to this case and its cited fix",
    "each key changes the window's selected sidebar item exactly as its sidebar action does from the same start (the script's oracle): the key wins over the focused surface, with no rebinding (Leo 2026-10-12)",
    "the start's tabs are the same at every key's settled checkpoint as at start: no key switches the pane's tabs instead",
    "Cmd-Opt-Left / Right are Ghostty's pane focus keys (schemas/keybindings/ghostty-reserved-keys.json), not sidebar keys",
    "every mutation has one receipt or one typed error (I1)"
  ],
  "teardown": [
    "quit the tagged app the run started",
    "verify its debug socket is gone",
    "end the tag's daemons (TagTeardown)"
  ],
  "untested": [
    "Leo's Karabiner sequences (Cmd-Shift-] / [, Ctrl-Tab) cycle the pane's tabs now; the script's SEQUENCES is empty",
    "real key-downs through cua-driver (--real): the case uses the app's key path (debug.key), as the script does by default",
    "the router's dry-run decision per key (debug.key dry_run) is not a case op; the settled selection is the check"
  ]
}
